1
00:00:00,984 --> 00:00:04,024
(Penny:)-Sorry. I'll get better.
-I know you'll try.

2
00:00:06,089 --> 00:00:08,659
(Leonard:)So, should we talk
about setting a date?

3
00:00:08,825 --> 00:00:11,365
(Penny:)Well, I'd like to pick one that works
with my brother's schedule.

4
00:00:11,528 --> 00:00:13,028
(Leonard:)Okay, and when would that be?

5
00:00:13,730 --> 00:00:16,370
(Penny:)Uh, 12 to 18 months from now,
depending on good behavior.

6
00:00:19,336 --> 00:00:21,786
(Amy:)-Hi, is Sheldon here?
-No, I thought he was with you.

7
00:00:21,939 --> 00:00:23,849
(Amy:)He was, but he stormed off.

8
00:00:24,007 --> 00:00:26,117
(Amy:)-Now he isn't answering his phone.
-What happened?

9
00:00:26,276 --> 00:00:28,386
(Amy:)He was really angry
that you suggested he move out.

10
00:00:28,545 --> 00:00:29,785
(Howard:)Oh.

11
00:00:29,947 --> 00:00:31,727
(Amy:)I also mentioned
that he and I could live together,

12
00:00:31,882 --> 00:00:34,552
(Amy:)but he was too mad at you to realize
what a great idea that is.

13
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:39,120
(Leonard:)Well, he's been having
a couple of tough days.

14
00:00:39,289 --> 00:00:40,389
(Leonard:)I'm sure he's fine.

15
00:00:40,557 --> 00:00:43,057
(Leonard:)He probably just needs
a little alone time to decompress.

16
00:00:43,227 --> 00:00:45,207
(Amy:)You're probably right.

17
00:00:45,362 --> 00:00:47,142
(Amy:)So, what are you guys doing?

18
00:00:49,466 --> 00:00:53,076
(Penny:)Well, Leonard cooked for me and now
we're just having a nice dinner,

19
00:00:53,237 --> 00:00:55,647
(Penny:)you know, as a newly engaged couple.

20
00:00:55,806 --> 00:01:02,026
(Amy:)That's nice.

